[Music]  from battling alongside xena to painting  with beeswax here's what the actor who  played gabrielle has been up to lately  just as xena warrior princess helped put  renee o'connor on the map it also  kick-started her love for directing the  actor got the opportunity to direct the  xena season 4 finale and she later  helmed an episode in season six  after her time on xena warrior princess  o'connor founded roc productions and  went on to direct award-winning shorts  as well as some lesser-known full-length  films she co-directed diamonds and guns  as her first feature film directing  credit while starring in the project and  acting as executive producer you  recognize me according to o'connor the  move from acting on screen in a tv show  for six years to the production side of  things came with a steep learning curve  she produced a number of shorts  including words unspoken which won her  awards for best short film and best  actress at the west hollywood  international film festival when asked  what inspired her to direct words  unspoken o'connor told film nut i wanted  to direct something where i didn't have  to compromise to a studio such as to a  television show i could really just be  authentic in my own voice and in my own  visions it seems like she ran with that  wish as o'connor went on to direct her  second feature film broken things a few  years later in 2015. in 2017 watch the  sky was released o'connor played a dual  role in the family sci-fi film appearing  on screen while also acting as executive  producer  somewhere between beasting out as  gabrielle on xena warrior princess and  diving into different roles on movie  sets renee o'connor tackled the biggest  job of all creating and raising a family  she married her first husband steve muir  while still playing gabrielle and she  gave birth to their first child miles  shortly after the series ended in 2001.  the transition to motherhood wasn't an  easy one in an interview with camera  conversations o'connor explained i had  been busy for so many years for six  years working 80 to 90 hours a week and  then suddenly that was all gone and it  was just a baby and myself  after her marriage to mirror ended  o'connor married jed sura who has  partnered with her on many projects the  two share a daughter iris sura o'connor  both of her children inherited the  acting bug performing in her production  watched the sky alongside their mom iris  also had a role in roc productions  infinity and miles was in an episode of  the show my life is murder  after the finale of xena warrior  princess renee o'connor acted in a  number of low-budget b movies and  monster films one such flick was alien  apocalypse in which she starred opposite  horror and b-movie legend bruce campbell  the film is exactly what it sounds like  an apocalypse movie that takes place  after aliens have taken over earth the  two stars shared a kiss in the film  which campbell deemed so wheat in a  tweet isn't she something unsurprisingly  fans were graced with this union of cult  icons because the two have a solid  connection with mr sam raimi executive  producer of hercules legendary journeys  and xena warrior princess and it's  thanks to campbell's long professional  relationship with raymie that he landed  the recurring role of atollicus well  let's hope he's at least as debonair and  charming as i am or no one will be  fooled  renee o'connor also branched out into  live theater she took on the role of  lady macbeth in 2002 but according to  broadway world she didn't fully get into  a theater career until 15 years later in  addition to playing lady macbeth more  than once o'connor has played the nurse  in a production of romeo and juliet in  which her son miles muir held the role  of romeo though she's had roles in  multiple shakespearean plays in classics  like annie mary poppins and the wizard  of oz she's also starred in more modern  dramas in 2017 o'connor joined the cast  of dinner with friends at littlefish  theater she has played a number of roles  at the venue including the lead and  steven dietz on clover road just like  her hollywood career o'connor expanded  her live theater one by sitting in the  director's chair she helmed a production  of romeo and juliet sharing the  experience with fans in an instagram  post of herself directing on stage  next renee o'connor founded her own  non-profit theater company house of  bards located in san pedro in addition  to producing she typically takes a dual  role either acting in or directing the  productions according to broadway world  house of bart's theater company's first  production was macbeth in 2019 starring  o'connor and her husband jed sura as the  leads surah co-founded the theater  company with o'connor and has been  partnering on projects since well before  its conception house of bards presented  its second play with romeo and juliet  the same production o'connor directed  which had its last show in may of 2022  renee o'connor's artistic ability goes  beyond the screen and stage during the  lockdown she updated her official  website with an art page full of  paintings she made she would use a  mixture of beeswax and resin crystals  combined with pigments to create layers  of translucent colors that form an  overall image this wasn't the first time  o'connor has demonstrated her love of  painting in an interview with hobo  trashcan she revealed that she used the  money she earned from selling paintings  to help fund her first production  venture diamonds and guns that film came  out in 2008 so it's clear that painting  has been another creative outlet for the  former xena warrior princess star for  quite some time  if you assumed that spending six years  opposite each other on a world-renowned  hit tv series would make renee o'connor  and lucy lawless pretty tight you aren't  wrong while the xena warrior princess  stars can go years at a time without  seeing each other they have nonetheless  stayed good friends following the series  when asked about their relationship in  an interview with the toronto star  lawless revealed that very much like  their xena warrior princess roles it's a  sisterhood it's beyond friends forged in  the heat of battle xena warrior princess  was filmed in new zealand lala's home  country and where she still resides  o'connor on the other hand is an  american who relocated to transform into  gabrielle for the series she returned to  the states after the show ended which  put quite the physical distance between  the two stars but they've always found  ways to reconnect  renee o'connor traveled to new zealand  during the lockdown to reunite with her  former co-star when she accepted a  one-off role in lawless's acorn tv  mystery series my life is murder in 2021  o'connor appeared in an episode as the  wife of a health guru who ends up dead  the xena warrior princess alums found  themselves going head-to-head in my life  as murder rather than fighting together  like the good old days a refreshing  change for the two friends according to  an interview the reunited stars gave to  entertainment weekly it had been a while  since they'd seen each other this  combined with o'connor wearing a mask  made it so lawless didn't even recognize  her at first despite that and the fact  that o'connor hadn't been on a tv set in  quite some time the on-screen reunion  was easy going it just felt like walking  into lucy's living room and having  friends over it was so charming and  loving and it was like that all the way  to the very end i actually had a little  withdrawal when i finished filming  my life as murder isn't the only recent  collaboration between the former xena  warrior princess stars prior to their  reunion on lucy lawless's show the two  actors reunited remotely for their  series 25th anniversary sci-fi fangirls  put together a five-episode podcast that  was a total blast from the past for both  fans and those involved in xena just as  stars like bruce campbell and ted raymie  return to talk about their time on the  show o'connor and lawless have their own  episode together in episode 2 of the  xena warrior princess 25th anniversary  podcast the two reminisced about all the  less than ideal conditions of filming  the series in new zealand lucy lawless  recounts the time rats were dumped on  her while filming an uncomfortable scene  saying she had them up her xena skirt  and spiders in her mouth while that  might sound like a horrifying day  looking back on the situation together  seems like it was a lot more fun for the  co-stars  rene o'connor and lucy lawless seemed to  have gone through the ringer when they  were filming xena warrior princess but  you wouldn't expect anything less from  two killer amazonian warriors as it  turns out the stars also became lesbian  icons after they appeared as xena and  gabrielle o'connor was voted lesbian  nation's most loved woman in 2006  beating out lawless who still came in  second in 2007 their places swapped the  series hints at a romantic relationship  between xena and gabrielle even though  it never became canon that the two were  together however after the series ended  lawless made the truth about the  relationship clear telling siriusxm in  2010 that xena and gabrielle were a  couple  when speaking to page six about the  lesbian undertones of xena warrior  princess o'connor said she felt that if  the show were on today the characters  would have no need to only hint at their  relationship are you in love with  gabrielle  [Music]  although it was only implied it was  still groundbreaking for the time  something that the lgbtq community could  latch onto as a kind of representation  in mainstream media  although gabrielle and xena's  relationship was a hot topic back when  the show was on the air the characters  are still very much beloved by their  loyal fan base o'connor and lawless have  both attended their fair share of  conventions for xena warrior princess  over the years giving the former  co-stars opportunities to catch up with  fans and each other fan events and  conventions take o'connor and lawless  all over the map but for two people who  live thousands of miles away from each  other they're pretty much the perfect  excuse to be in the same city during  multi-day events the two actors tend to  appear on the same day to greet fans and  answer questions this was exemplified by  creation entertainment's 2022 salute to  xena event which celebrated the series  quarter-century milestone both actors  enjoy interacting with the convention  crowds during the 2018 fan expo canada  in toronto lawless thrilled attendees by  calling o'connor her screen wife all  these years post xena the two stars  still have a great time together and  with their fans  [Music]

